<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand III, Grand Duke of Tuscany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1769">1769</a>–<a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a>, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> prince who lost Tuscany to the French in 1799. In compensation he was given the secularised Archbishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> as an electorate in 1803, then exchanged it in 1805 for the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a>, which he ruled until 1814. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fall he was restored to Tuscany, governing it until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="Ferdinand III, Grand Duke of Tuscany" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Dorffmeister · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Dorffmeister_-_Gro%C3%9Fherzog_Ferdinand_III._(1769-1824),_Sohn_von_Leopold_II.,_in_seiner_Bibliothek_sitzend,_Kniest%C3%BCck.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
